---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Profile</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    Master's student in Information Management & Business Analytics at The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen (QS Top 50).
    Product Manager with internship experience at Tiger Brokers (derivatives trading) and Hupu (user research & growth).
    Skilled in translating user insights into product solutions, with a strong focus on fintech UX, AI product design, and data-driven decision making.
    IELTS 7.0, fully English-taught throughout undergraduate and graduate studies.
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="M.S. in Information Management & Business Analytics"
      subtitle="2025.09 - 2027.08 at The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen (QS Top 50)"
    >
      Core courses: Systems Design & Analysis, Project Management, Big Data Analytics, Web Analytics, Database Management, Mathematical Analysis
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="B.S. in Information Management & Information Systems"
      subtitle="2021.09 - 2025.06 at Southwestern University of Finance and Economics (Project 211)"
    >
      Delaware Data Science College
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Product Manager Intern — Derivatives Trading"
      subtitle="2025.11 - 2026.03 at Tiger Brokers (Beijing Yixinxiangshang Technology), Product Department"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-4 space-y-2">
        <li><b>Order Search UX Redesign:</b> Users could only search orders by exact ticker code, causing frequent support tickets. Analyzed customer complaints and identified the core mental model as "options OF what I bought" rather than "what options I bought." Designed a 3-layer solution: filter optimization + fuzzy Chinese/English name search + derivative-underlying asset association. Daily PV increased from 24K to 28K, related complaints dropped to zero.</li>
        <li><b>HK Stock Options Paper Trading (0-to-1):</b> Designed simulated matching logic for both real-time and delayed market data scenarios. Benchmarked against Futu and Interactive Brokers. Post-launch achieved 100+ weekly simulated trades, creating a complete learn → practice → live trading path for new users.</li>
        <li><b>Core Trading UX Consistency Governance:</b> Identified that 3 order pages × 2 platforms = 6 inconsistent interaction standards. Unified interaction specs across all product categories. Projected feature retention rate improvement from 28% to 30%.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="User Research Intern"
      subtitle="2024.12 - 2025.04 at Hupu (Shanghai Kuanghui Network Technology), User Research Center"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-4 space-y-2">
        <li><b>Off-Site Content Distribution Platform:</b> Led the design of an automated content distribution system integrating task publishing, AI-powered content production, channel distribution, data monitoring, and auto-settlement. Designed a "base + performance" dual-incentive model for scalable distribution.</li>
        <li><b>Content Production Strategy:</b> Built a data-driven + editorial topic selection mechanism. Leveraged AI tools for automated content production, supporting 6,000+ pieces distributed across 500+ channels within 24 hours.</li>
        <li><b>User Growth Results:</b> Single campaign published 3,288 pieces of content, generating 12.64M impressions and 8,449 effective new-user search referrals, validating scalable acquisition feasibility. Trial run achieved 10,000 new users per week.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Projects</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Khrushchev Simulator — AI-Driven Historical Strategy SLG"
      subtitle="2026.03 (Independent Project)"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-4 space-y-2">
        <li>Built a core loop of "intelligence generation → natural language negotiation → intent parsing & numerical settlement → world state emergence." Players negotiate among 5 factions and 31 characters through real dialogue, supporting 10 endings.</li>
        <li>Completed model selection based on role-play capability, Chinese quality, and token cost. Defined 3 AI metrics (numerical overflow rate, instruction compliance, character consistency) to drive prompt iteration. Overflow rate: frequent → zero; compliance: 85% → 95%+.</li>
        <li>Designed "presentation layer AI generation + logic layer hard numerical hosting" separation architecture to mitigate hallucination risks. Converted prompt injection into immersive NPC defiance/questioning experiences.</li>
        <li>5-version closed beta with 5 core strategy gamers. Average 20+ rounds per session, all players voluntarily started a second playthrough.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Skills</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc md:columns-5 columns-2 mx-6">
    <li>Office Suite</li>
    <li>Figma</li>
    <li>Axure</li>
    <li>SQL</li>
    <li>Python</li>
    <li>R</li>
    <li>Git</li>
    <li>Prompt Engineering</li>
    <li>Harness Engineering</li>
    <li>Data Analysis</li>
    <li>User Research</li>
    <li>Competitive Analysis</li>
    <li>Product Design</li>
    <li>IELTS 7.0</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
